WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.506
- [Interviewer] All right, Tony.

00:00:09.506 --> 00:00:10.530
- [Tony] How's it going?

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.090
- [Interviewer] Tony,
where you from originally?

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:12.923
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:12.923 --> 00:00:15.283
- My origin from Victorville, California.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.853
San Bernardino County.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.353
- [Interviewer] Did you have
both your parents growing up?

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.640
- I had both my parents growing up,

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.460
and just my father, he was
absent from most of my life.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.820
He was in the military
and was very violent,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.373
and he left my side about nine years old.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.583
- [Interviewer] When you say
he left, where did he go?

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.730
- He went to prison, federal prison,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:51.730
because he was manufacturing
drugs and stuff like that,

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.693
so, he was taken away from us.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:03.030
- [Interviewer] And how was
your childhood otherwise?

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.143
- It was good.

00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:09.450
I grew up as a Christian guy.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:14.450
I was in the music industry
with a band and stuff,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.970
Christian band, and that's what I did

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:19.803
with most of my childhood, was--

00:01:19.803 --> 00:01:21.040
- [Interviewer] So religion was a big part

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:21.873
of your upbringing?

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:23.447
- Yeah, it was a part of my life.

00:01:23.447 --> 00:01:25.440
It was a big part of my life,

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.440
and with my extra time, I
was doing my schoolwork,

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.450
and I was in track and
field, and wrestling,

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:37.460
and I had a pretty good childhood.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.930
My mom, she was always devoted to us,

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:45.453
and she never really concentrated
anything else but us.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.280
And all I can do is thank
my mom for raising us

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.000
to best way she could, you know?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.010
There was six of us and single parent.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.820
She went to school, she got educated,

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.390
and I don't know how she did it,

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.553
but a single mom, it would raise us all,

00:02:07.753 --> 00:02:11.140
and we lived pretty poor,
you know what I mean?

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:14.753
A good meal for us was Top Ramen.

00:02:16.438 --> 00:02:19.503
That's pretty much what it was.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.650
Although it was tough for her,

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.563
and I appreciate her and I
know she had a hard time,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.650
but my childhood was rough.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:35.150
I was brought up fairly well as in,

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.010
I'm a 3.9 student.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.950
I almost got my 4.0.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.820
Like within all my
years, I was a good kid.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:49.320
I was one of the best I could say

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.130
because that tool I would
always thrive for was,

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.053
I was really competitive.

00:02:55.023 --> 00:02:57.313
I always wanted to be the best.

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:04.530
And I did that but, I made some decisions

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.530
along down the road which,
I became who I am today.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.327
Some of my friends would ask me,

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.647
"What happened, what made that change?"

00:03:19.007 --> 00:03:21.970
I made it, and now I got to live with it.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.943
But, I can go from negative to positive.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.923
Within my experiences that
I have experienced now,

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:33.430
I plan on somehow turning it into

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:38.190
like I see myself helping the
youth or anything like that.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.270
Like now, within my experiences in prison

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.030
and the things that I went through,

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.120
I believe I can turn it
into something positive

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:52.120
and help other kids
that have the background

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:58.370
of the gang-life or drug use,
and all so forth like that.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.441
That's what I plan on doing now

00:04:03.441 --> 00:04:05.760
because this wasn't the plan,

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.543
but sometimes life throws
a curveball at you.

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:16.851
And somebody smart, he told me,

00:04:16.851 --> 00:04:18.317
"Do you know the difference

00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:22.257
"between a Major League Baseball player

00:04:22.257 --> 00:04:24.697
